# External API

Signed access for a partner system. `X-API-KEY` selects the integration. The partner holds the matching RSA private key, and AIPT stores the public key on that row.

Base path: `/api/external`

![Partner signs the request, then AIPT checks the 120 second window, public key, nonce, and IP allowlist before returning the client list.](external-api-flow.jpg)

## What you send

`GET /api/external/clients`

| Header | Required | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Accept` | yes | `application/json` |
| `X-API-KEY` | yes | The `api_key` stored on the integration |
| `X-TIMESTAMP` | yes | Unix time in seconds, digits only |
| `X-NONCE` | yes | Unique string for this request |
| `X-SIGNATURE` | yes | Base64 RSA-SHA256 signature of the canonical string |

The timestamp must be within 120 seconds of the server clock, ahead or behind. Each nonce can be used once for that integration, and the server remembers it for 5 minutes. Send a new nonce on every call, including retries.

If `allowed_ips` is set on the integration, the request IP must be in that list. Separate addresses with commas or spaces. An empty list allows any IP.

## Canonical string

Five lines, joined with `\n`. No trailing newline after the hash.

```text
GET
/api/external/clients
<X-TIMESTAMP>
<X-NONCE>
<sha256 hex of the raw body>
```

`GET` has an empty body. Its hash is always:

```text
e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
```

Sign that exact string with the private key using SHA-256, then base64-encode the signature. The query string is not part of the signature. This endpoint does not use one.

AIPT loads the active row whose `api_key` equals `X-API-KEY`, then checks the signature with that row’s public key.

## Setup

Run the migration so `api_integrations` exists, then create a key pair and store the public key.

```bash
openssl rand -hex 32
openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out partner-private.pem
openssl pkey -in partner-private.pem -pubout -out partner-public.pem
php artisan migrate --path=database/migrations/2026_09_23_092938_create_api_integrations_table.php
```

`openssl rand -hex 32` prints the 64-character `api_key`. Store it on `api_integrations.api_key` and send that same value in `X-API-KEY`. `partner-public.pem` goes in `public_key`. Keep `is_active` true. `partner-private.pem` stays with the partner.

`name` is a label. `rate_limit` is stored and not enforced. `allowed_ips` is optional. `last_used_at` is updated after a request passes the checks.

## Calling the endpoint

```bash
API_KEY="the api_key stored on the integration"
TS=$(date +%s)
NONCE=$(openssl rand -hex 16)
BODY_HASH=e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
CANON=$(printf '%s\n%s\n%s\n%s\n%s' "GET" "/api/external/clients" "$TS" "$NONCE" "$BODY_HASH")
SIG=$(printf '%s' "$CANON" | openssl dgst -sha256 -sign partner-private.pem | base64 -w 0)

curl -sS "https://your-host/api/external/clients" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-KEY: $API_KEY" \
  -H "X-TIMESTAMP: $TS" \
  -H "X-NONCE: $NONCE" \
  -H "X-SIGNATURE: $SIG"
```

`printf '%s\n' ...` would add a newline after the hash. Do not use it. The server signs the string with no trailing newline.

```php
$apiKey = 'the api_key stored on the integration';
$method = 'GET';
$path = '/api/external/clients';
$timestamp = (string) time();
$nonce = bin2hex(random_bytes(16));
$bodyHash = hash('sha256', '');

$canonical = implode("\n", [$method, $path, $timestamp, $nonce, $bodyHash]);

$privateKey = openssl_pkey_get_private(file_get_contents('partner-private.pem'));
openssl_sign($canonical, $rawSignature, $privateKey, OPENSSL_ALGO_SHA256);

$headers = [
    'Accept' => 'application/json',
    'X-API-KEY' => $apiKey,
    'X-TIMESTAMP' => $timestamp,
    'X-NONCE' => $nonce,
    'X-SIGNATURE' => base64_encode($rawSignature),
];
```

## Success body

HTTP 200. `errors` is null. `meta` is omitted on this endpoint.

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "status": 200,
  "message": "Clients retrieved successfully",
  "data": [
    {
      "client_name": "Acme",
      "is_duplicate": true,
      "departments": [
        { "department": "Accounting", "id": 12 },
        { "department": "Litigation", "id": 4 }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": null
}
```

Rows are grouped by the lowercased, trimmed name. `client_name` is the first spelling in that group. `is_duplicate` is true when the group has more than one source row. `departments` lists each source `department` and its `id`.

The three department labels this endpoint emits are `Accounting`, `Litigation`, and `Patent`.

## Error body

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "status": 401,
  "message": "Request expired.",
  "data": null,
  "errors": null
}
```

| HTTP | Message | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 401 | `API key is required.` | `X-API-KEY` is missing |
| 401 | `Invalid API key.` | No active integration has that `api_key` |
| 401 | `Valid timestamp is required.` | `X-TIMESTAMP` is missing or not all digits |
| 401 | `Request expired.` | Timestamp is more than 120 seconds from the server |
| 401 | `Nonce is required.` | `X-NONCE` is missing |
| 401 | `Signature is required.` | `X-SIGNATURE` is missing |
| 401 | `Invalid signature.` | Signature does not match that integration’s public key |
| 401 | `Request replay detected.` | This integration already used that nonce |
| 403 | `IP address is not allowed.` | Request IP is outside `allowed_ips` |
| 429 | Laravel default body | More than 60 requests in a minute from the same IP |

The 429 response comes from the global `api` limiter and does not use the envelope above. Its message is `Too Many Attempts.` and it may include a `Retry-After` header.

Other methods on this trait, when a later endpoint uses them, keep the same envelope:

| Method | HTTP |
| --- | --- |
| `createdResponse` | 201 |
| `acceptedResponse` | 202 |
| `noContentResponse` | 204, empty body |
| `badRequestResponse` | 400 |
| `notFoundResponse` | 404 |
| `conflictResponse` | 409 |
| `validationResponse` | 422, `errors` is a map of field to message list |
| `tooManyRequestsResponse` | 429, plus `Retry-After` when a retry delay is set |
| `serverErrorResponse` | 500 |
| `serviceUnavailableResponse` | 503 |

A paginated payload puts the items in `data` and page fields in `meta`: `per_page`, `current_page`, `last_page`, `total`, `from`, `to`, `has_more`. Cursor pages use `next_cursor` and `prev_cursor` instead of a page number.

## Browser calls

CORS allows `https://app.example.com` and the headers `Content-Type`, `Accept`, `X-API-KEY`, `X-TIMESTAMP`, `X-NONCE`, and `X-SIGNATURE`. A server-to-server caller does not use CORS.

## Data currently loaded

| `department` in the response | Table | Name column |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Accounting | `clients` | `client_name` |
| Litigation | `li_clients` | `client_name` |
| Patent | `pt_clients` | `client_name` |

`clients` is the trademark client table. Accounting records in `acc_clients` are not included. The patent query filters `deleted_at`, and `pt_clients` has no `deleted_at` column, so a signed request fails when that query runs until the filter or the table changes.


